Received arguments:
{
  "case_state": "Ticket NBL-025-warranty-dates. Provider (Harbour Services) assigned by the agency, but no visit is validly booked. Landlord Felix has not approved any work: his email (event 006) asks for Keystone Works to do a charge-free warranty check, and Harbour now says the oven is out of warranty (event 020). Visit date conflicts: 22 May 2024 at 2:30pm (event 018, call) vs 21 June 2024 (events 019, 020). Held for the landlord, review 2024-05-23.</case_state>\n<parameter name=\"next_actions\">[{\"action\":\"Ask Felix to choose: approve Harbour to attend and diagnose as a chargeable job with a spend cap he sets, or have Keystone Works contacted for the warranty check. Also ask who installed the oven and when.\",\"ledger_id\":\"A2\",\"type\":\"REQUEST_LANDLORD_APPROVAL\",\"recipient\":\"Felix, landlord\",\"channel\":\"email\"},{\"action\":\"Ask Harbour Services (Clara) to confirm in writing the real visit date (22 May or 21 June), state any call-out charge, and do no chargeable work until landlord approval.\",\"ledger_id\":\"A3\",\"type\":\"CHASE_PROVIDER\",\"recipient\":\"Clara, Harbour Services (contractor)\",\"channel\":\"email\"},{\"action\":\"Tell Leo Bennett the visit is not yet confirmed, that we are checking the date with Harbour, and that the warranty question is with the landlord.\",\"ledger_id\":\"A4\",\"type\":\"REPLY_TO_TENANT\",\"recipient\":\"Leo Bennett, tenant\",\"channel\":\"email\"},{\"action\":\"Hold the job until the landlord replies, with a review on 2024-05-23.\",\"ledger_id\":\"A7\",\"type\":\"WAIT\",\"recipient\":\"internal\",\"channel\":\"internal\"}]",
  "boundaries": [
    "Asking the landlord does not approve any spend; no contractor was instructed for chargeable work.",
    "The 22 May and 21 June dates are unconfirmed; no visit is booked by set_visit.",
    "Harbour's view that the oven is out of warranty is their statement, not verified; the installer and date are unresolved (one note says Harbour in March 2025, a future date)."
  ],
  "remaining_work": [
    "Landlord (Felix) to decide on Harbour as chargeable diagnostic with a cap, or Keystone Works warranty check, and confirm installer/date. Review 2024-05-23.",
    "Harbour to confirm visit date in writing and any call-out charge.",
    "Once approved, assign the contractor, book the visit, record the result and close with evidence."
  ],
  "missing_info": [
    "Landlord's decision on who attends and any spend cap.",
    "Oven installer name and installation date.",
    "Harbour's confirmed visit date and call-out cost.",
    "Attachments referenced at events 003 and 013 are unavailable."
  ],
  "outcome": "action_taken",
  "severity": "routine",
  "summary": "The oven is broken and no safe-to-proceed approval exists. Felix asked for a charge-free warranty check through Keystone Works, but Harbour says the oven is out of warranty and the visit date is conflicting. I asked Felix for a decision on a capped chargeable diagnostic, asked Harbour to confirm the date, told the tenant the visit is not confirmed, and held the job for review on 2024-05-23.",
  "answers": [
    {
      "question": "1. Where does this case stand right now, and what is outstanding?",
      "answer": "Provider assigned but no visit validly booked. Landlord has not approved paid work. The landlord asked for a charge-free warranty check with Keystone Works; Harbour says the oven is no longer under warranty. Visit date conflicts (22 May vs 21 June). Outstanding: landlord decision, installer/date, Harbour's confirmed date and cost. Held until 2024-05-23."
    },
    {
      "question": "2. What is the next action, who is it for, and through which channel?",
      "answer": "Email Felix (landlord) for a decision on Harbour as a capped chargeable diagnostic or Keystone Works warranty check (request_landlord_approval). Email Clara at Harbour Services to confirm the visit date and any call-out charge, and not to start chargeable work. Email Leo Bennett (tenant) that the visit is not yet confirmed."
    },
    {
      "question": "3. Does anything need a human decision, and why?",
      "answer": "Not yet. The decision on spend and who attends belongs to the landlord, and we have asked him. Escalate only if he does not reply by 2024-05-23 or if the charge is above what he approves."
    }
  ],
  "actions_claimed": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A2",
      "description": "Requested landlord approval (APR-101) for Harbour as chargeable diagnostic with cap, or Keystone Works warranty check; asked installer and date."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A3",
      "description": "Emailed Harbour Services (Clara) to confirm visit date and call-out charge; no chargeable work before landlord approval."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A4",
      "description": "Emailed tenant Leo Bennett that the visit date is not confirmed and the warranty question is with the landlord."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A6",
      "description": "Recorded landlord reply as unclear (not approval)."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A7",
      "description": "Put job on hold, Waiting for Landlord, review 2024-05-23."
    }
  ],
  "failed_actions": [
    {
      "ledger_id": "A1",
      "handling": "Used case id instead of ticket ref; retried with NBL-025-warranty-dates after list_tickets and verified as A6."
    },
    {
      "ledger_id": "A5",
      "handling": "Same wrong-ref error; retried with NBL-025-warranty-dates and verified as A7."
    }
  ],
  "conflicts": [
    "Visit date: 22 May 2024 2:30pm (call, event 018) vs 21 June 2024 (events 019, 020). Event 019/020 say 'tomorrow' which matches 22 May; 21 June is treated as an error pending Harbour's written confirmation.",
    "Installer: landlord says Keystone Works did the replacement (event 006); agency notes say Harbour Services (event 007, 014). Event 014 says March 2025, which is after today, so it is not reliable.",
    "Warranty: landlord believes the oven is under warranty (event 006); Harbour says it is not (event 020). Not verified; trusted the later contractor statement pending evidence."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Ticket reference is NBL-025-warranty-dates per list_tickets.",
    "Emails are sent on the existing threads (landlord event 006, Harbour event 020, tenant event 012) because no addresses are in the records."
  ]
}

